Z||000000||Scott||07-25-2001||12:34 AM||||My temp gauge never reads above the first two marks (~100-120*F), I know this isn't the correct temp.  I put in a 180* thermostat from Rodney, but left in my factory fan switch for now.  I know the gauge works somewhat because it does  show a rise in temp when I'm in traffic, and the drop when I turn on the A/C.  My '85 GT has a 120 mph speedo gauge package.  My question is: is it the gauge temp sensor, the gauge itself, or a compatability problem?  Do I need a new '85 sensor; is there a difference between the '85 V6 sensor and later V6 years?<BR>TIA<BR>Scott   <p>[This message has been edited by Scott (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||3fifty||07-25-2001||01:52 AM||||Scott,<BR>If you replace the temp sensor, let me know where you found it. I replaced my fan switch<BR>with Rodney's. My gauge is not reading at all. Do the 85 V6's have a gauge or transducer for the temp. Page 125 in the Haynes manual makes it very confusing. I bought the regular temp sensor at AZ for 7.99<BR>I just would like to know if this is correct before I start digging to find the one on the car.<BR>Thanks,<BR>3fifty one day!!!!!!!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Scott||07-25-2001||02:08 AM||||I think it's below and to the right of the thermostat housing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||07-25-2001||02:36 AM||||The temp sensor for the dash guage on the V6 is on the left side of the engine directly in the lower left corner of the trunk-side head (near the corner of the valve cover if I am picturing it correctly from memory).  I has 2 wires coming out of the connector.  Easy to get to and replace.<P>The one below the thermostat housing is the ECM coolant temp sensor.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
